  "id": "COMPOUND:40572 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Caragasinin B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to NH-6 through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Caragasinin B acts as a target for two different compounds, M059J and Plakortide N, both of which are targets of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, a compound that ultimately targets NH-6. This indicates a shared mechanism of action, where Caragasinin B is involved in the signaling or regulatory processes that ultimately lead to the activation of NH-6. The presence of multiple pathways converging on NH-6 suggests a potential role for Caragasininin B in modulating the activity of these downstream targets, possibly through a common intermediate or a shared cellular function. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network and the importance of understanding the interplay between these compounds in determining their functional outcomes.",
